/-!
# Principal specialization of the actual Laurent module

For a surjective structural algebra map with kernel generated by the displayed
scalar, the actual localized scalar cokernel equals the target module's local
length in `ENat`, including infinity. This comparison requires no flatness.
Regularity in the base separately kills the localized scalar kernel and gives
the integer-valued Euler identity. Finite-length interpretation retains the
stated target Noetherian and minimal-support hypotheses. Algebraic-simplex
specializations are downstream adapters.
-/
